        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "Label": "UNLABELLED",
            "content": "Acute compartment syndrome after medial gastrocnemius tear is very rare. It can involve the superficial posterior compartment alone or progress to involve all the 4 compartments of the lower legs. Those patients with high pain tolerance and minor trauma can lead to delayed presentation. Immediate fasciotomy is the treatment of choice."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "LEVELS OF EVIDENCE",
            "content": "Therapeutic Level IV, Case Study."
          }
